---
import PageLayout from "../../../components/PageLayout.astro";
import { releases } from "../../../data/releases";
---
<PageLayout lang="en" active="download" title="Download — Linxira OS">
    <a href="/en/" class="back">← Back to Home</a>
    <h1>Download Linxira OS</h1>
    <p>Current build is <b>2026.10.31-r2</b> (October 31 batch, fix round 2): the GRUB environment block now lives on the ESP, fixing btrfs <code>grubenv</code> errors such as <code>sparse file not allowed</code>; install validation rejects a leftover btrfs env; BIOS installs no longer create one. This is a test image, not a stable release.</p>

    <div class="note">
      <p><strong>This build only changes the GRUB boot path.</strong> UEFI installs keep <code>grubenv</code> on the ESP; install validation rejects or removes a leftover btrfs <code>/boot/grub/grubenv</code>. <strong>This is not a stable release</strong>: build, static checks, and CI passed, but no real UEFI boot test has been run yet; run <code>linxira-update</code> once after first boot.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dl-card">
      <h3>{releases.iso.filename}</h3>
      <div class="meta">{releases.iso.sizeHuman} · Desktop / headless installer · x86_64</div>
      <a class="dl-btn" href="https://gitcode.com/BOHUYESHAN-APB/Linxira-os" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open GitCode Repository →</a>
      <a class="dl-btn ghost" href={`https://gitcode.com/BOHUYESHAN-APB/Linxira-os/src/main/${releases.iso.filename}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">ISO File Page</a>
      <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;font-size:0.85rem;color:#64748b;">In the GitCode repository, click the ISO file → Download button (large file served via Git LFS).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dl-card">
      <h3>{releases.wsl.filename}</h3>
      <div class="meta">{releases.wsl.sizeHuman} · WSL2 distro (CLI-first toolchain + WSLg-capable GUI tools) · x86_64</div>
      <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#94a3b8;margin-bottom:0.9rem;">Linxira WSL puts the whole Linxira toolchain inside Windows' WSL2: <strong>systemd</strong> enabled, the signed [linxira] repository tracks updates directly, and <code>linxira-config stack</code> completes Python / Java / LaTeX / containers in one command — CLI, TUI, and GUI (WSLg) forms, a full Linxira environment without reinstalling.</p>
      <a class="dl-btn" href="https://github.com/Linxira-OS/linxira-wsl/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Releases →</a>
      <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;font-size:0.85rem;color:#64748b;">Import with <code>wsl --import linxira C:\wsldata {releases.wsl.filename} --version 2</code>, then <code>wsl -d linxira</code>. systemd is enabled; see the Release assets for the SHA256 file.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Checksums</h2>
    <pre><code>{`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS

# SHA256 (${releases.iso.filename}):
${releases.iso.sha256}  ${releases.iso.filename}

# WSL image (${releases.wsl.filename}): see *.sha256 assets on the GitHub Release`}</code></pre>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--faint);">All sizes use decimal units: 1 GB = 10⁹ bytes, 1 MB = 10⁶ bytes.</p>

    <h2>Installation</h2>
    <p>See the <a href="/en/docs/install/" style="color:#20B8B0;">installation guide</a>: write the ISO to a USB drive, then choose <strong>KDE Plasma</strong> (recommended), <strong>Headless (full toolset)</strong> or <strong>Headless (minimal)</strong> at the desktop step. COSMIC is still listed but should be treated as experimental.</p>

    <h2>Known issues in this build</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The GRUB environment block now lives on the ESP</strong>: UEFI installs use <code>EFI/linxira/grubenv</code>, so btrfs <code>/boot/grub/grubenv</code> no longer triggers <code>sparse file not allowed</code>; <code>GRUB_DEFAULT=0</code> prevents <code>grub-mkconfig</code> from creating a btrfs env. BIOS installs no longer create one, and therefore do not remember the last selection.</li>
      <li><strong>Install validation is now explicit</strong>: a missing ESP env, a missing <code>saved_entry</code>, or a leftover btrfs <code>/boot/grub/grubenv</code> fails the install instead of producing a system that errors on first boot.</li>
      <li><strong>No real hardware boot test yet</strong>: r2 has build, static checks, and CI, but UEFI boot and last-selection behavior still need real-machine confirmation.</li>
      <li><strong>Test image</strong>: not recommended as the only production system; run <code>linxira-update</code> once after first boot.</li>
      <li><strong>The first <code>linxira-update</code> may report an unsynced repository</strong>: from <code>linxira-update 0.1.10</code> the tool retries <code>pacman -Sy</code> and re-detects automatically; older versions need one manual <code>sudo pacman -Sy</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Audio pop on power transitions</strong>: headphones or speakers may click briefly at power-on; this is hardware-level noise and is not addressed here.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="note">
      <p><strong>No old versions</strong>: Arch Linux is a rolling release, so an image only reflects the repositories of its build day. <strong>Old images are not retained or offered — only each version's SHA256 is recorded</strong>. Images are built roughly every 25–45 days; always use the current version on this page.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
      <p>Note: the ISO is an aggregate work — kernel GPL-2.0-only, system components under their own licenses, first-party tools MIT/GPL-3.0. The SHA256SUMS file is stored alongside the ISO in the GitCode repository; WSL images live in the linxira-wsl repository Releases.</p>
    </div>
<style>
    h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; color: #20B8B0; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.8rem; }
    li { color: #94a3b8; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    pre { background: #0a0f1a; border: 1px solid rgba(51,65,85,0.5); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; overflow-x: auto; margin: 1rem 0; }
    pre code { background: none; color: #cbd5e1; padding: 0; }
    .dl-card { background: rgba(30,41,59,0.5); border: 1px solid rgba(32,184,176,0.3); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.6rem 1.8rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    .dl-card h3 { color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
    .dl-card .meta { color: #64748b; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .dl-btn { display: inline-block; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #20B8B0, #F36F5D); color: white; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.8rem 2rem; border-radius: 10px; text-decoration: none; margin: 0.3rem 0.5rem 0.3rem 0; transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s; }
    .dl-btn:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(32,184,176,0.35); text-decoration: none; }
    .dl-btn.ghost { background: transparent; border: 1px solid rgba(51,65,85,0.8); color: #e2e8f0; font-weight: 500; }
    .dl-btn.ghost:hover { border-color: #20B8B0; color: #20B8B0; }
    .note { background: rgba(32,184,176,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(32,184,176,0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; margin: 1.2rem 0; }
    .note p { color: #cbd5e1; margin: 0; }
  </style>
</PageLayout>
